WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.241
Uh-oh! Who are you?

2
00:00:07.242 --> 00:00:11.181
I'm a rattlesnake.

3
00:00:11.182 --> 00:00:15.466
Rattlesnakes are reptiles.

4
00:00:15.467 --> 00:00:18.115
Where do you live?

5
00:00:18.116 --> 00:00:23.052
Rattlesnakes live in North and South America.

6
00:00:23.053 --> 00:00:28.227
We live in prairies, forests, and deserts.

7
00:00:28.228 --> 00:00:31.403
What's on your tail?

8
00:00:31.404 --> 00:00:34.663
That's my rattle.

9
00:00:34.664 --> 00:00:42.318
We shake our rattles to warn enemies.

10
00:00:42.319 --> 00:00:45.316
What do you eat?

11
00:00:45.317 --> 00:00:49.623
We mostly eat small animals.

12
00:00:49.624 --> 00:00:55.134
We love rabbits, mice, and prairie dogs!

13
00:00:55.135 --> 00:00:58.241
How do you find food?

14
00:00:58.242 --> 00:01:03.652
Our tongues are shaped like forks.

15
00:01:03.653 --> 00:01:07.648
They help us smell prey.

16
00:01:07.649 --> 00:01:13.217
We can sense heat from prey too.

17
00:01:13.218 --> 00:01:16.818
You have big fangs!

18
00:01:16.819 --> 00:01:21.651
We use our fangs to bite.

19
00:01:21.652 --> 00:01:25.948
The bite kills our prey.

20
00:01:25.949 --> 00:01:30.081
Then we swallow the animal whole!

21
00:01:30.082 --> 00:01:33.740
Do rattlesnakes shed their skin?

22
00:01:33.741 --> 00:01:38.523
Yes, we shed our skin as we grow.

23
00:01:38.524 --> 00:01:42.959
We rub against rocks to loosen it.

24
00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:47.076
Then we crawl right out of our skin!

25
00:01:47.077 --> 00:01:49.436
Good-bye.

26
00:01:49.437 --> 00:01:56.052
Good-bye, Rattlesnake!

